This product is a readable PyTorch re-implementation of the Quest sparse
decoding path that HiSparse uses for Qwen3-30B-A3B.

Portions of this product are derived from SGLang
(https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang), Copyright 2023-2026 SGLang Team,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.  The derived logic follows
the `hisparse_quest` branch at commit
e568f8a362b4ae3a597b28b75716309814aa33fb, in particular:

  python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/sparsity/algorithms/quest_algorithm.py
  python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/sparsity/factory.py
  python/sglang/srt/managers/hisparse_coordinator.py
  python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/flashinfer_quest_backend.py
  python/sglang/srt/layers/attention/flashinfer_hisparse_backend.py
  python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/hisparse.cuh

The code was rewritten in plain PyTorch (no Triton / CUDA / FlashInfer),
restructured, and documented; see docs/upstream_mapping.md for a
function-by-function correspondence and the list of intentional changes.

The Qwen3-MoE architecture follows the Hugging Face `transformers`
implementation (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers,
Apache License 2.0).

References:
  Quest: Query-Aware Sparsity for Efficient Long-Context LLM Inference,
    Tang et al., ICML 2024, arXiv:2406.10774.
  HiSparse: Scaling Sparse-Attention Decoding with Hierarchical KV Cache
    Management, arXiv:2608.07009.
